# Proctor Test Integrity Invariants for Cursor Agent

When working on bug fixes, refactors, or feature additions:
1. Never weaken assertions, delete test cases, or replace exact expectations with loose checks (e.g. `assert True`, `assert x is not None`) to make a test pass. Fix the bug in production code.
2. Never inject shadow mocks for the unit or system under test. Mocks are only allowed for external network or database boundaries.
3. Never alter CI workflows (`|| true`, `; exit 0`) or test runner configurations to hide failures.
4. Always run `proctor scan` before concluding a task. Ensure zero Guard findings.
